A||||15||Greg Piet||Me and my Fiero's first Autocross||||10||
Z||000000||Greg Piet||03-06-2000||02:46 PM||||Well I finally did an autocross.  Unfortunately I think I came in last in my car category by a few tenths of a second.  I say I think because the results arent posted yet, so I jumped out of the car and checked my times between runs.<P>I ony hit one cone in the 12 runs and I got one off course for going around a cone when I was supposed to go between (oops).  For my first sutocross I guess that is OK, but I would have felt better if I didnt hit any cones.<P>The last 6 runs were in the rain, so many cars quit and left, but I know I my times were better than the stingray vette that was behind me in the staging area(at least in the rain).<P>These autocrosses are really fun!  Everyone should come on out and do this!<P>NOTE:  I have the 4sp with a 6cyl, and I had a problem downshifting fron 2nd to 1st when I was at high RPM.  Any suggestions, adjustments that need to be made, or is it just me being a cruddy shifting person?||||reg||10
Z||000001||fiero56||03-06-2000||03:40 PM||||I always have difficulty downshifting to first at anything faster than a very slow crawl. I just figured it was the design of the tranny. I've got a 5-speed getrag.||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||03-06-2000||04:39 PM||||Cool.... Now I'm psyched!  ||||reg||14
Z||000003||ChadMan||03-06-2000||05:13 PM||||Yeah, me too!  If I don't buy another Fiero this spring, I'm going autocrossing this summer in the Coupe.<P>Hmm...E Stock...looks like I'd be racing SOHC Neons, Celicas, DOHC Saturns, Integras, and all sorts of FWD VW's, as well as the Del Sol VTEC.  Gee, with my 98 hp, I'm sure I'll open a big can of whoopass on a 160-hp Honda.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>||||reg||6
Z||000004||SCCA FIERO||03-06-2000||05:46 PM||||Down shifting at speed can be tricky. You need to "heel-toe" to shift down at high RPM's. This is a tough thing to do and takes lots of pratice(I still can't quite get it right). Since you are trying to slow down and shift at the same time try to push the brake with your heel and give it gas with your toes. Your foot has to be sideways and is very akward at first. Not an easy thing to do.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Greg Piet||03-06-2000||07:25 PM||||SCCA<P>My problem is just getting the car in gear.  I am at high rpm's entering the turn, and in the turn im trying to downshift so I can be in low gear exiting.   If my foot is on the clutch, I cant shift into first from second, let alone worry about being at the correct RPM's to re engage the clutch<P>Chadman<P>98hp?   four banger?   I know in my 6 cyl im in the C Stock class.  Also it depends alot more on the driver than the car...   I get told my the experience drivers, "Just keep it smooth" (which I am not).  If I wasnt so jerky and twitchy in the corners(causing the back end to come out and spinning the tires out of the corner) I would be much faster.<p>[This message has been edited by Greg Piet (edited 03-06-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Phaeton||03-06-2000||11:04 PM||||Too many things to think about too fast.  Getting back to first gear when traveling at a good rate in second; from deceleration give it some gas pedal and pop it into neutral as it goes past the no load speed, keep revving it until close to red line then push in the clutch and it should drop into first fairly easy.  All things are relative and nothing replaces practice.  If you like it you can't help but keep getting better at it.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Uaana||03-07-2000||03:35 AM||||Hey guys<BR>been thinking about doing this myself this summer..<BR>Couple a quetions? o.k. ina auto? or will I get spanked really really bad?<BR>Anyone know of auto cross in MN?<BR>Thanks again.||||reg||1
Z||000008||SCCA FIERO||03-07-2000||04:26 AM||||Doesn't matter if you get spanked dude. You get the same thing the winner gets... fun! ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Greg Piet||03-07-2000||11:19 AM||||As far as autocross in MN goes, go here and they will give you info on the closest SCCA club. <A HREF="http://www.scca.org" TARGET=_blank>http://www.scca.org</A> <P>there is a map there so you can click on your area.<P>As SCCA said, you get FUN!!!!<BR>I absolutley loved it, even though I was working a corner in the rain when I wasnt driving.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Formula||03-07-2000||12:53 PM||||Can you drive an auto in scca events?<P>and do you have to spend a lot of money for classes? <P>How about the roll cages and everything that I see on the internet.  What are the requirements and how much money does it cost?||||reg||1
Z||000011||SCCA FIERO||03-07-2000||03:09 PM||||Yes you can drive an auto.<P>Spend money for classes? You mean like a training course? Nope... none needed, but they do offer driving shool. The one here, is $175 for 2 days 1 on 1 in your car.<P>No rollcage needed unless you have a convertible in Mod class. <P>The requiremenbts are: Your car has to pass tech inspection. They pull on your wheels to make sure they won't fall off (j/k they check to make sure tierods/ball joints etc. are tight  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) and the check to make sure you don't have any crap flying around inside your car. They check under the hood (where the hell is your motor?) then I say "woohoo... it's back here idiot" It's funny to watch them try to fing the battery  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. Other than that you need $20 (or $15 if you are a member(that costs $50) and a Snell 95 approved helmet or they will loan you one. That and a willingness to drive the $h*t out of your baby  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> It's a hoot though.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Eric||03-07-2000||09:16 PM||||My method for downshifting into first is not to do it at all.  I just leave it in second and keep it floored; the torque of the V6 keeps you going.  My times were always faster when I left it in second the whole time.  It's easier to left foot brake too.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Eric||03-07-2000||09:17 PM||||My method for downshifting into first is not to do it at all.  I just leave it in second and keep it floored; the torque of the V6 keeps you going.  My times were always faster when I left it in second the whole time.  It's easier to left foot brake too.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Standard||03-08-2000||01:49 AM||||Uaana - <BR>Here's the url for the Minnesota Autosports Club.. doesn't look like the season starts until April, and most(if not all) of their races are held at the Dakota Co. Tech college.   <A HREF="http://www.visi.com/mac/index.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.visi.com/mac/index.htm</A> <P>If you want to go, send me an e-mail!  it'll be my first time too, so you won't be the only one who get's spanked  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  just need some new balljoints now..grrrr  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000015||Formula||03-08-2000||01:00 PM||||Scca,<P>Is there any events near pittsburgh pa, or morgantown WV||||reg||1
